How I'm understanding the logic you described
Org structure: One Org Admin role with visibility across all stores and warehouses. Right now: 1 main store, 1 warehouse, 1 sub-store — but the system should let you add more stores/warehouses later without new features, just new records.
Stock requests between locations: A store that's low/out of stock raises a request (product, brand, quantity). Other locations see it; whoever has stock responds; requester accepts one; a transfer with driver/transport info gets created; receiving side confirms receipt; only then does stock move (deduct from sender, add to receiver).
Customer credit ("udhar"): You can sell without full payment. There's a configurable default limit for how much credit a customer can be given without approval; above that, it needs approval before the sale can proceed.
Black sales/commission: A product's normal price and the actual price charged to a customer can differ (e.g., 100 vs 150). The 50 difference isn't shown in the main UI. If someone facilitated the sale and takes a commission (e.g., 15) out of that difference, the store nets the remainder (35). This needs its own tracking separate from the regular ledger.
Transfers generally: Not just store-to-store — also store-to-warehouse, warehouse-to-store, warehouse-to-warehouse. All combinations should be possible.
Sales reporting: Product-wise sales and total sales.

