That's everything. Here's the full picture consolidated in one place so you can sanity-check it all at once before I turn it into the actual data model.
Roles
Org Admin & Org Manager — equal power: both authorize black sales, both see the black ledger/inventory, both can move stock between official and black.
Store Admin / Store staff — normal operations only, zero visibility into black.
Sub-store — identical permissions to main store, no hierarchy.
Warehouse — purely internal, no customer-facing Sales screen; staff have the same permission tier as store staff.
Driver — own entity, selected from the full driver list at transfer time; sees every transfer (including black ones) as identical/normal.
Locations
Store and Warehouse are the same underlying entity, just type-flagged — a warehouse isn't locked to one store.
Currently 1 main store + 1 warehouse + 1 sub-store, but the model supports adding more of either freely.
Customers & credit
Customer type (Regular/New/Shop/Big Customer) and sale type (Normal/Credit/Black) are independent fields — any combination is valid.
Credit limit is per customer, auto-tracked as a running balance (rises on credit sale, falls on payment). Over-limit requires Org Admin/Manager approval before the sale proceeds.
Official inventory — requests & transfers
Low/out-of-stock triggers a request (product, brand, quantity) broadcast to all locations.
Multiple locations can respond; requester picks. Partial fulfillment is supported cumulatively — request stays open until the total accepted meets the original quantity.
Accepted → transfer with driver assigned → stock sits as in-transit (counted at neither location) → status moves Sending → Sent → Confirm/Received, with Confirm/Received done by the receiving location's staff, not the driver → on confirmation, deduct from sender / add to receiver.
Works for every combination: store↔store, store↔warehouse, warehouse↔warehouse.
Requester can withdraw a request; acceptor can reject it — both only before dispatch.
Black sales & commission
A sale can be priced above official price; the difference ("black") is hidden from the main UI.
A facilitator (system user or off-system name) can take a cut — commission auto-calculated, store keeps the remainder. Tracked as a running Commission Payable ledger per facilitator, marked "Paid" when settled.
Only Org Admin/Org Manager can create a black sale or see the black ledger.
Black inventory
Fully separate stock pool per product per location, invisible to everyone but Org Admin/Manager.
Received independently (product, qty, cost, source, date) — never touches the official count.
A black sale deducts only from this pool; official stock count never moves.
Org Admin/Manager can convert stock either direction (black↔official); each conversion logs an adjustment entry visible only to them.
Black stock can transfer between locations while staying black — admin-only direct move, no store-level request/response, but still physically driven through Sending → Sent → Confirm/Received.
Org Admin/Manager get a full parallel report on black stock (on-hand, value, movement history).
Reporting
Separate reports: product-wise, total, store-wise, warehouse-wise, salesperson-wise, payment-method-wise, credit-vs-cash.
Black ledger, black inventory report, and Commission Payable report — Org Admin/Manager only.
True Total report — merges official + black revenue into one real number, Org Admin/Manager only.
Currency
Multi-region capable, but one org runs on a single currency, set once at the org level.
Connectivity
Always online for this phase; no offline/sync logic built now.
Out of scope this phase
Customer returns / credit notes.
Stock adjustments (damage / expiry / loss).
Notifications & documents
In-app notifications for low stock, pending approvals, transfer status changes.
Debtor Note, Statement, Delivery Note — all shareable PDFs.
